{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534558-is-mage-the-awakening-eurocentric","id":1534558,"title":"Is Mage the Awakening Eurocentric?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-22T08:44:23-07:00","id":1534558,"title":"Is Mage the Awakening Eurocentric?","content":"I know some people who have played Mage the Awakening complain about how it's too eurocentric with it focus on atlantis, which trivialize other magical tradition around the world. While I don't really see how it could trivialize other magical tradition, but I couldn't agree on whether it eurocentric or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-22T09:13:26-07:00","id":1534560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534558-is-mage-the-awakening-eurocentric#post1534558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know some people who have played Mage the Awakening complain about how it's too eurocentric with it focus on atlantis, which trivialize other magical tradition around the world. While I don't really see how it could trivialize other magical tradition, but I couldn't agree on whether it eurocentric or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps that could be said of the first edition, and even then the Order books and the Magical Traditions book tried to give depth and nuance to the actual Atlantis beliefs and what other parts of the world had to say.<br /> <br /> Second edition on the other hand? Not Eurocentric as far as I am concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-22T09:14:26-07:00","id":1534561,"title":"","content":"What do you think make the the second edition not eurocentric, while the first edition was eurocentric?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-22T11:35:40-07:00","id":1534563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534558-is-mage-the-awakening-eurocentric?p=1534560#post1534560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps that could be said of the first edition, and even then the Order books and the Magical Traditions book tried to give depth and nuance to the actual Atlantis beliefs and what other parts of the world had to say.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Secrets of the Ruined Temple, which blasted apart any idea there was a monolithic Atlantis myth by showcasing a vast range of beliefs about the Time Before from around the world and across history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-22T11:54:11-07:00","id":1534564,"title":"","content":"2e is pretty emphatic that &quot;Atlantis&quot; is mostly parabolic, with the Diamond being the ones who treat it the most literally. And even there it's more that their Mystery Cult roots tend toward Greek, iirc? So the idea of a forerunner Mage society before the Fall often ends up with specific cultural trappings, but the core of their belief is that the actual &quot;Atlantis&quot; is pretty divorced from today.<br /> <br /> There's a bit more of a leaning toward the US and Europe in terms of setting fluff, I guess? But every book mentions beliefs and traditions from other regions of the world. world.k that up to the main player base being from the US/the Americas and Europe (an assumption on my part, admittedly), which means it's easier to introduce the game using familiar surroundings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 04-22-2024, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-22T21:40:31-07:00","id":1534572,"title":"","content":"Awakening heavily focuses on western culture and the western image of the wizard, but it does not really deal much with western magical traditions. Other magical traditions are trivialized even more than western magical traditions are, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-23T11:32:26-07:00","id":1534600,"title":"","content":"There are probably some conceptual biases by virtue of largely being written by American and British people (as far as I know), but Second Edition both puts more effort into placing &quot;Atlantis&quot; into context and then downplaying it anyway, and the core book contains a number of sample locations found throughout the world to emphasize the more international quality as well as regional differences. Those latter aspects are given even more development in one of the source books.<br /> <br /> The metaphysical background of the setting draws upon multiple belief systems, and in character the major organizations of the Awakened are explicitly syncretic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T20:55:01-07:00","id":1534677,"title":"","content":"OP, if your friends thought it was too Eurocentric for them you're probably not going to be able to argue them out of that, since that's their genuine impression of the game. It's definitely at least a little bit Eurocentric and even a bit's too much for some people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-29T12:30:09-07:00","id":1534917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534558-is-mage-the-awakening-eurocentric#post1534558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know some people who have played Mage the Awakening complain about how it's too eurocentric with it focus on atlantis, which trivialize other magical tradition around the world. While I don't really see how it could trivialize other magical tradition, but I couldn't agree on whether it eurocentric or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never saw it that way as even in the 1st edition that the nation of Atlantis was an imperfect recall of their past and that they weren't sure what the name of there city truly was and using the name was a good title as anything and we did have later sourcebooks in the 1st edition that covered other groups that were awakened and most likely had there own creation stories. I saw it as a non issue and left as a mystery that never would be truly solved as the Seers of The Throne and their masters did an effective job of remaking the world in there own image.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-29T18:07:22-07:00","id":1534926,"title":"","content":"I would say not, since one of the most interesting parts of <i>Tome of the Pentacle</i> is that it shows how mage society might recognize certain symbols, beings and phenomena in common. Simultaneously, how they organize themselves, interpret the Mysteries and build their body of knowledge is unique to each culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T14:12:46-07:00","id":1535038,"title":"","content":"Tomes Of The Watchtowers and Magical Tradition really show how each culture had common themes for magic and it didn't confuse the issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T18:38:38-07:00","id":1535046,"title":"","content":"I'll admit, we can't lean <i>too</i> heavily on in-character explanations to evaluate the subject, given some of the external context. &quot;Atlantis&quot; as a choice for the magical precursor probably ought to be considered against the real world sentiments that led to it being popularised as such a thing in both fiction and pseudohistory in the first place. And the Pentacle Orders might also still slant a bit in that direction in some of their ideas and general iconography.<br /> <br /> But I'd also say that this was the sort of thing the game was aware about in itself from quite early on, and a lot of efforts were made towards actively redressing that. I do think that in some early books like Tome of the Mysteries, there's a certain tone of &quot;okay, I know how this looks, but just hear me out&quot;. A comprehensive look does give a more rounded out picture as well as the tools to go even further on one's own initiative, but I wouldn't blame (or downvote) anybody for looking at some of the stuff presented at the surface level and coming around with questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T23:18:27-07:00","id":1535052,"title":"","content":"I find it interesting that no one has mentioned how the clarification of 2nd Edition came in parallel to the Dark Eras of To The Strongest, at least overtly. The big reason for the mention is that it was properly conceiving of the origin of the Diamond Sect as both the oldest still standing sect for the main game, and in tying it's foundation to the Hellenistic World, a lot of the game design and terminology came into focus.<br /> <br /> TO be particular about this, while the unified Greek nation has it's influences on the Diamond in design, and consequently for much of the game as a design flow from there, the majority of it's initial foundation is rooted in the Middle East and the Indian sub-continent and the peoples thereof, represented by the Persian Karpani, the Egyptian Weret-Hekau Hemka, and the Indian Mantra Sadhaki-from the evolution and methodology from this determination and how it affected 2nd Edition's development, that alone would incline the game towards more a Middle Eastern/Eastern influence.<br /> <br /> To compound matters is the fairly quick addition post Dark Eras's initial pitches and Awakening 2nd's release was the stretch goal for Princes of the Conquered Lands, centering on the Shona Awakened of South Africa at the beginning of Portuguese colonialism in the area. The goal was an excuse to challenge and reframe the text and set a standard moving forward for the franchise by taking a fairly different and an initially unplanned on worldview and seeing how well the model constructed for Awakening worked with what we know of the Shona people's drastically different approach-Shakespeare in the bush but with wizards-but then allowing what came out of the clashes to reshape Awakening going forward by letting the Shona warp what was constructed for Awakening, rather than try and cram the Shona into Awakening's model. Awakening's archetypal model with it's already non-Eurocentric outlook actually handled that pretty well, but the experiment compounded on the design decisions made from the non-Eurocentric approach of the core, and curved idle details further away from such models, which would see expression in the nitty gritty in the gameplay mechanics of the Signs of Sorcery(rooted in decisions connected to Tome of the Pentacle, about to be discussed), and in the in-game history by increasing the cultivation of the Diamond (again, used as the the main reason for most of the dialect Awakening due to it's age and prominence) to make the next major layers of Great Cults to contribute to that core ideology and vocabulary being the Chinese Fang Shih, Eblaite(Syrian) Maskim, and the Judean Synhedrion in, as promised, the Tome of the Pentacle.<br /> <br /> Tl;dr up to this point, it would be more accurate to call Awakening Middle Eastern-centric, with it's in game decisions reflecting choice to move away from eurocentric models.<br /> <br /> That said, there is a point where there's no denying that the Grecian infleunce can't be ignored-Brookshaw himself once described the core of the game as Neo-Platonism by way of Theosophy-and a lot of Eurocentrism roots itself in the Grecian and Italian Pennisulas. But on the other hand, the game is designed for a mostly &quot;Western&quot; audience in mind, on account that White Wolf and then Onyx Path having a lot of their reach limited to those regions, and that audience is inclined to better understand Neo-Platonic thought rather than the workings of Hindi religious and occult practices. And to be honest, to have even the core shy away from it and to have it's ongoing path be rooted in distinctly non-European beliefs and occult practices really pays out.<br /> <br /> I will not be accounting for 1st Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-02T09:06:55-07:00","id":1535076,"title":"","content":"Chronicles of Darkness, and pretty much every Storyteller derived game, is Americentric even down to the presumed availability of firearms. 2e is much better than 1e was, and 1e was nowhere near WW's worst example (fuck the Scion 1e weapon table only listing specific models of forearm), but it's still there. Anything suggesting vampires can't easily move between cities probably doesn't take into account how densely populated Europe can be.<br /> <br /> Which is fine, the developers are primarily pulling from their own cultures and trying to avoid stereotyping others. The game will never be truly universal even if only due to a limited number of pages.<br /> <br /> As to Atlantis itself being a Eurocentric element, yes but as has been stated it's been massively de-emphasised and turned into the idea of 'the time before' and 'the awakened city' with less specific ties. The idea's still there, but the gnostic elements have taken centre stage. Which I'll point out <i>is still a relatively Eurocentric element</i>, and arguably a bigger deal than Atlantis as it's entwined with the setting's metaphysics and cosmology.<br /> <br /> I'm just hesitant to say that gnosticism is a strictly Eurocentric element as I don't know enough about most religions or philosophies to say if similar ideas crop up regularly all over the place or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-02T09:54:53-07:00","id":1535080,"title":"","content":"Neo-Platonism and Gnosticism definitely inform the depiction of the Supernal, but they don't resemble it entirely, and I do think there was an extent to which other religious ideas of transcendental reality (such as the Vedic) was already informing the concept. It lends credibility to the depiction of the backstory for the Atlantean sect provided from To The Strongest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T01:27:18-07:00","id":1536557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534558-is-mage-the-awakening-eurocentric#post1534558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know some people who have played Mage the Awakening complain about how it's too eurocentric with it focus on atlantis, which trivialize other magical tradition around the world. While I don't really see how it could trivialize other magical tradition, but I couldn't agree on whether it eurocentric or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does not &quot;trivialize other magical traditions&quot;. It outright says that Sleeper magical traditions are wrong - all of them, Western and Eastern. Then it presents the universal Truth with capital letters, and says that everything all Sleeper cultures are doing is seeing glimpses and parts of it, while distorting it with Lie anyways. Then it says that some people do see the Truth, and understand which parts of their cultural heritage were right all along.<br /> <br /> It doesn't spend too much time describing how exactly different cultures see their Paths and Orders, but it does a good attempt in Tome of Pentacle. There probably would be more of it, but sadly, game line inofficially ended along with CofD at large. The best we can do is try to paint those pictures themselves, while trying to be as true and respectful to the cultural sources as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T12:27:23-07:00","id":1536575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534558-is-mage-the-awakening-eurocentric?p=1536557#post1536557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does not &quot;trivialize other magical traditions&quot;. It outright says that Sleeper magical traditions are wrong - all of them, Western and Eastern. Then it presents the universal Truth with capital letters, and says that everything all Sleeper cultures are doing is seeing glimpses and parts of it, while distorting it with Lie anyways. Then it says that some people do see the Truth, and understand which parts of their cultural heritage were right all along.<br /> <br /> It doesn't spend too much time describing how exactly different cultures see their Paths and Orders, but it does a good attempt in Tome of Pentacle. There probably would be more of it, but sadly, game line inofficially ended along with CofD at large. The best we can do is try to paint those pictures themselves, while trying to be as true and respectful to the cultural sources as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is true that Mage: The Awakening demonstrates an exceedingly patronizing attitude towards mortal magical traditions, but the text of Mage: The Awakening does not really line up with some of the other Chronicles of Darkness books. It seems to clash most obviously with Second Sight. The text of Mage: The Awakening suggests that mortal magical traditions are almost completely wrong, but Second Sight does not depict them in that light. Indeed, thaumaturges are depicted as having greater insight than common mortals, and their magic is often depicted as being different from Supernal magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T14:36:30-07:00","id":1536587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534558-is-mage-the-awakening-eurocentric?p=1536575#post1536575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is true that Mage: The Awakening demonstrates an exceedingly patronizing attitude towards mortal magical traditions, but the text of Mage: The Awakening does not really line up with some of the other Chronicles of Darkness books. It seems to clash most obviously with Second Sight. The text of Mage: The Awakening suggests that mortal magical traditions are almost completely wrong, but Second Sight does not depict them in that light. Indeed, thaumaturges are depicted as having greater insight than common mortals, and their magic is often depicted as being different from Supernal magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a bit unnuanced even before I start gesticulating wildly in the direction of the entire Pentacle Order (canonically the single largest of all Orders) with the creed of &quot;Humanity is Magical&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T20:03:08-07:00","id":1536599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534558-is-mage-the-awakening-eurocentric?p=1536575#post1536575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is true that Mage: The Awakening demonstrates an exceedingly patronizing attitude towards mortal magical traditions, but the text of Mage: The Awakening does not really line up with some of the other Chronicles of Darkness books. It seems to clash most obviously with Second Sight. The text of Mage: The Awakening suggests that mortal magical traditions are almost completely wrong, but Second Sight does not depict them in that light. Indeed, thaumaturges are depicted as having greater insight than common mortals, and their magic is often depicted as being different from Supernal magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Verlan, not for the first time it would behoove you to clarify whether you are talking about Mage as it currently exists or as it existed when Second Sight was released <i>eighteen years ago</i> with an altogether different metaphysical framing and design philosophy.<br /> <br /> Second Sight spends most of the first six pages of its Thaumaturges chapter presenting options for what the true nature of thaumaturgy is, and its subsection explaining the difference between thaumaturges and mages relies on an explanation of how Supernal magic works that hasn't been accurate since at least the start of Second Edition if not sooner \u2014 the Supernal Realms are only places when perspective is being used to experience them as one and the Atlantean traditions are ahistorical creations derived from commonalities between different cultural mythologies and magical discoveries.<br /> <br /> There's magic in the world that people can perform without being Awakened or otherwise made intrinsically magical. The Awakened know this. They also know that a lot of the narratives people have around magic is urban legend and broken telephone and disinformation by virtue of having tools for magical scrutiny as the easiest forms of magical power available to them, so they can usually tell pretty easily when the overactive window spirit that's rattling your porch glass is not, in fact, Grandpa's ghost trying to send a message to his grieving children. Much of this has little to do with saying Jainism Is Totally Wrong, Actually, and it is going to take more than vague gestures and unsubstantiated claims for statements like &quot;Awakening suggests that mortal magical traditions are almost completely wrong&quot; to go unchallenged if your metric is more stringent than &quot;characters with some amount of filtered divine power can exploit the plasticity of phenomenal experience in a way not accessible to those more firmly anchored in reality.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T15:21:04-07:00","id":1536650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534558-is-mage-the-awakening-eurocentric?p=1536587#post1536587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's a bit unnuanced even before I start gesticulating wildly in the direction of the entire Pentacle Order (canonically the single largest of all Orders) with the creed of &quot;Humanity is Magical&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The magical nature of humanity is a key tenet of the Free Council, but the Free Council focuses more on the dynamic nature of human culture rather than adhering to models of revelation. That does not really work with all mortal magical traditions, as some do focus on revelation. In the setting, Supernal magic has primacy, and the cosmology of the setting is depicted as being more true than the cosmologies of mortal magical traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T15:58:27-07:00","id":1536651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534558-is-mage-the-awakening-eurocentric?p=1536599#post1536599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Verlan, not for the first time it would behoove you to clarify whether you are talking about Mage as it currently exists or as it existed when Second Sight was released <i>eighteen years ago</i> with an altogether different metaphysical framing and design philosophy.<br /> <br /> Second Sight spends most of the first six pages of its Thaumaturges chapter presenting options for what the true nature of thaumaturgy is, and its subsection explaining the difference between thaumaturges and mages relies on an explanation of how Supernal magic works that hasn't been accurate since at least the start of Second Edition if not sooner \u2014 the Supernal Realms are only places when perspective is being used to experience them as one and the Atlantean traditions are ahistorical creations derived from commonalities between different cultural mythologies and magical discoveries.<br /> <br /> There's magic in the world that people can perform without being Awakened or otherwise made intrinsically magical. The Awakened know this. They also know that a lot of the narratives people have around magic is urban legend and broken telephone and disinformation by virtue of having tools for magical scrutiny as the easiest forms of magical power available to them, so they can usually tell pretty easily when the overactive window spirit that's rattling your porch glass is not, in fact, Grandpa's ghost trying to send a message to his grieving children. Much of this has little to do with saying Jainism Is Totally Wrong, Actually, and it is going to take more than vague gestures and unsubstantiated claims for statements like &quot;Awakening suggests that mortal magical traditions are almost completely wrong&quot; to go unchallenged if your metric is more stringent than &quot;characters with some amount of filtered divine power can exploit the plasticity of phenomenal experience in a way not accessible to those more firmly anchored in reality.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize. I understand that many of my comments likely seem repetitive, and that I can be frustrating to argue with. I will try to explain my thought processes more thoroughly.<br /> <br /> In regards to the matter of editions, I am speaking about both editions of Awakening. I brought up Second Sight as it dealt with the topic of mortal magic and its relationship with Awakened magic more completely than I have seen since. It is very much a relevant supplement to bring up when discussing this matter, and I find it unusual that the 2e did not address thaumaturgy more thoroughly. That is why I brought it up even though the cosmology of the Supernal changed between editions. The Supernatural Merits of 2e are also relevant.<br /> <br /> Your last paragraph actually touches on one of the reasons why I began to discuss this matter. Frankly, the portrayal of the Awakened as being more correct about the true nature of the universe than mortals are is ridiculous. There is a serious attitude of condescension towards mortal religion and magic in much of Awakening. This is not unique to Awakening, and it is very much present in many other role-playing games. I would not even have that much of a problem with it were it not for the constant jabs levelled at religions and various subcultures. Second Sight was unique in that it was probably one of the most respectful works that White Wolf ever produced that related to the matter. That is one of the main reasons why I brought it up.<br /> <br /> I mostly bring this matter up to due to the patronizing air of many of the books. I could understand if it was something like Ars Magicka, in which a specific cosmology is utterly assumed and there are no attempts to act like the nature of the universe is up for debate. I just cannot take a role-playing game seriously when it has a parasitic relationship with the objects upon which it is based.<br /> <br /> I have seen this for years, and recently, I have felt like commenting on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T16:42:24-07:00","id":1536653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534558-is-mage-the-awakening-eurocentric?p=1536651#post1536651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, the portrayal of the Awakened as being more correct about the true nature of the universe than mortals are is ridiculous. There is a serious attitude of condescension towards mortal religion and magic in much of Awakening. [...] I would not even have that much of a problem with it were it not for the constant jabs levelled at religions</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you give us a specific example that would be a bit easier to engage with?<br /> <br /> Like, before anything to do with the Free Council, I used the word &quot;unnuanced&quot;, because to my mind the subject is more complicated than that even within the boundaries of this being a game with a horror premise of hidden truth about reality.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head, there is the Ministry of Paternoster. A group of Seers of the Throne dedicated to the ideal of infiltrating Sleeper religion and choking out anything about them that is more than the oppressive dogma of the Father. <br /> <br /> Implicit in the premise is that there is actually something worthwhile within these faiths, or else there would not need to be anything for the Seers to suppress.<br /> <br /> At the same time, there's more to what can be oppressive about them than what the Seers bring.<br /> <br /> Like, as a random example... Latter Day Saint churches may bring a sense of genuine spiritual fulfilment to their members, but disfellowship is still a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 05-31-2024, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T19:47:41-07:00","id":1536658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534558-is-mage-the-awakening-eurocentric?p=1536651#post1536651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, the portrayal of the Awakened as being more correct about the true nature of the universe than mortals are is ridiculous. There is a serious attitude of condescension towards mortal religion and magic in much of Awakening. This is not unique to Awakening, and it is very much present in many other role-playing games. I would not even have that much of a problem with it were it not for the constant jabs levelled at religions and various subcultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Verlan. This is exactly what I meant when I referred to vague gestures and unsubstantiated claims. If you've seen it for years you should be able to point to specific examples at least at the scope of &quot;read this section from this book and tell me the vibes aren't off.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T21:17:22-07:00","id":1536659,"title":"","content":"Hell, the Silver Ladder may well be the Order that is most hostile towards (or at least incompatible with) other religions on the face of it, and their First Edition book had a section dedicated to description of how this creates dramatic tension in the form of unresolved schools of thought and debate within the Order. There <i>is</i> a position offered that the straightforward orthodoxy ought to be accepted directly and people divest themselves of their prior beliefs, which is clearly framed as not satisfactory to all members.<br /> <br /> This following in the wake of the signature setting including a prominent (mostly thearch) cabal of dedicated Puritans of all things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-01T12:11:23-07:00","id":1536677,"title":"","content":"To be fair the moment you become a supernatural being of some sort is going to make you totally rethink your religious biases and make you take a closer look at other cultures beliefs and wonder what is truly correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T05:44:51-07:00","id":1536739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534558-is-mage-the-awakening-eurocentric?p=1536575#post1536575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is true that Mage: The Awakening demonstrates an exceedingly patronizing attitude towards mortal magical traditions</div> </div> </div> </div>You could remove &quot;magical traditions&quot; there. You could say that Awakening demonstrates an exceedingly patronizing attitude towards Sleepers in general. Because, well, they are Asleep. They don't see the Truth. They live in the Lie. And, <i>mostly</i>, they can't do anything about it - other than Awaken, which sufficiently removes them from normal human experience so that they become patronizing towards mortals in general - <i>at best</i>, because, you know, they could just go into direction of not even bothering to patronize and just exploit.<br /> <br /> That's the horror of that game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534558-is-mage-the-awakening-eurocentric?p=1536575#post1536575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but the text of Mage: The Awakening does not really line up with some of the other Chronicles of Darkness books. It seems to clash most obviously with Second Sight. The text of Mage: The Awakening suggests that mortal magical traditions are almost completely wrong, but Second Sight does not depict them in that light. Indeed, thaumaturges are depicted as having greater insight than common mortals, and their magic is often depicted as being different from Supernal magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, as you probably know, Chronicles of Darkness is a constructor. Second Sight is <b>not</b> written with Mage: The Awakening at mind; the reverse is true as well. Different game lines often contradict each other factually and thematically, being their own universes. If Storyteller decides to bring them together, it's up to him to resolve those conflicts.<br /> <br /> Second, there is wrong and wrong. From point of view of Diamond, Fallen magical traditions are wrong, because they are not True with capital letters - they are not Supernal, or at least, their Supernal origins are sufficiently distorted by Lie and Pancryptia to deny them status of being True. From point of view of Free Council, Fallen magical traditions are wrong, because they are not yet there - they are seeds of inspiration which could one day become powerful enough to change Above, but not yet.<br /> <br /> Both of those do not deny that Fallen magical traditions exist, and sometimes they do real (still Fallen, but <i>real</i>) magic. Of course, thaumaturges have greater insight than common mortals - not only because they have said real magic, but also because by virtue of having it, they are Sleepwalkers and able to see and remember Truth. But both of those doesn't change the fact that in Awakening, there is objective Truth written in Heavens, and Fallen magical cultures isn't it - it <i>can't be</i>, otherwise it wouldn't be Fallen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1534558-is-mage-the-awakening-eurocentric?p=1536575#post1536575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, the portrayal of the Awakened as being more correct about the true nature of the universe than mortals are is ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's the basic premise of the game. It's right there, in the words &quot;Sleep&quot; and &quot;Awaken&quot;. Awakened are more correct about the true nature of the universe, because they saw the Truth of it, and now they can't unsee it. They see through Lie built by tyrant-kings of the Creation, and because of that, they can override it, if only for a while.<br /> <br /> That's not a suggestion to feel smug and superior in that knowledge (though many many Awakened do exactly that). It's a suggestion to feel the terror of it. You know <i>exactly</i> how broken, unfair and hostile the universe is, and you know <i>exactly</i> how powerless individual person is against that. The question is - what are you going to do about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","user":"Dark Archon","date":". 06-03-2024, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T08:07:43-07:00","id":1536744,"title":"","content":"Well said Dark Archon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T05:55:50-07:00","id":1536797,"title":"","content":"The Supernal Realms constitute a &quot;Truth&quot; with a capital letter in a kind of cosmological sense, but I think it's a mistake to read this as a definitive statement on Supernal things having more reality than things of the &quot;Fallen&quot; World. Even mages with the greatest level of investment in the idea that the Supernal is innately superior have to recognise that there are things that originate within their world (or possibly other neighbouring ones that made their way in), and the relationship these have with the Supernal can be difficult to grasp and raise a lot of questions. It's a complicated world out there, and they've gathered enough information on it to not just dismiss everything that isn't Supernal as patently inferior. This is reinforced in the text of the Second Edition core book in the opening paragraphs of the section titled &quot;Fallen Worlds&quot;.<br /> <br /> It should also be noted that &quot;Fallen World&quot; is an ideological term for what mages otherwise describe cosmologically as the Phenomenal World. That the world they inhabit exists physically isn't what makes it Fallen; mages understand that there was always a Phenomenal to a Supernal, and that indeed the two are interdependent on one another rather than set in a strict hierarchy. Presumably those who go deepest into the weeds of theory and exploration think that the Phenomenal World always contained occult phenomena distinct from direct Supernal power.<br /> <br /> The world is made Fallen only by the rise of the Exarchs and end of the Time Before. The presence of the Abyss and oppressive presence of Supernal Tyrants creates a more inhibited world, but the hold of those things is not absolute. And while mages might think that the influence of the Lie cannot be discounted from ideas and institutions that rose from under it, it's really only the most extreme of them (largely disavowed by their fellows) who think that absolutely everything from Sleepers is tainted because of that.<br /> <br /> Because that's another thing that's part of the equation; while there are things that manage to have varying degrees of Supernal influence, for various reasons, in spite of the reign of the Exarchs, things don't only have value if they evince Supernal understanding. There are plenty of mages who can look at a belief system in magic or spirituality or what have you and think that it has value in its own right, even if only for what it means to the people participating it, let alone if it's capable of having phenomenal results.<br /> <br /> Besides, it should be noted that the nature of the Supernal is technically more of a theoretical framework that has vogue among the largest segment of Awakened society than something described to the reader as objective fact. It's a highly sophisticated theory, benefiting from centuries of refinement and with a lot of practical applications to show for it. But it doesn't cover everything, and Tome of the Pentacle not only depicts a part of the world that sees it in very different terms, it includes some Mysteries that give some legs to that as a very alternative idea of what mages see with their Sight and accomplish through their imagos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T16:06:50-07:00","id":1536814,"title":"","content":"In a sense the Supernal isn't a worlds it is merely a description of the Phenomenonal world. It is a Truth in that it describes things on a deeper level than usually accessible, but then each path will see that Truth differently, and take different meanings away from the same thing - at least for things that aren't Abyssal Untruths - and the powers of a Mage are to alter the Truths that they can see, imposing new Truths.<br /> <br /> This doesn't make any claim about the truth of sleeper beliefs, just as describing the mechanism of action of flowering plants attracting pollonators doesn't change the enjoyment a person may get from smelling the roses once in a while.<br /> <br /> Those are two seperate and unrelated things. The Phenomenal actually exists, meanwhile the Supernal is merely a set of symbols describing the Phenomenal... An infinite set of symbols filtered through the paths and individual limits of a mage.<br /> <br /> And even with that supposed Truth, mages don't know what happens to souls when a person dies (or where they come from when someone is born). There are real limits to what a Mage can do/comprehend.<br /> <br /> But mainly, I don't see describing something (Supernal Truth) and being something (the Phenomenal existence of sleeper culture) is somehow in conflicted...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}